# Example environment variable file for contributor onboarding.
#
# This repository currently does not require any runtime environment variables
# for local development or production builds.
#
# If you do need custom settings locally, copy this file to .env.local and
# add variables there. `.env.local` is ignored by git, so your local secrets
# will not be committed.
#
# Example usage:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# See: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/guides/environment-variables
